<title>USA: Arco cuts U.S. Light Louisiana Sweet posted price.</title>
<headline>Arco cuts U.S. Light Louisiana Sweet posted price.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Arco said it cut the price it will pay for U.S. Light Louisiana Sweet crude oil by 25 cents a barrel, effective today.</p>
<p>The decrease brings the new price for LLS to $21.00 a barrel.</p>
<p>The price for West Texas Intermediate remains unchanged at $21.00. Other grades, West Texas Sour and Oklahoma Sweet, were also unchanged at $18.75 and $19.15, respectively.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
</text>
